# Round XXIX Track B — POS pin for the Dict.has_key / .contains_key
# oracle-only aliases (they are NOT in DICT.methods at
# src/ir/lowering/builtins.rs; only .has() / .contains() are). The
# aliases live in the oracle at typecheck.rs and are whitelisted in
# the ratchet via OK_ORACLE_ONLY. This fixture pins their continued
# TYPE-CHECK resolution post-widening (the runtime alias-vs-canonical
# discrepancy — has_key/contains_key print "0" instead of "true" — is
# a pre-existing bug in the LIR alias routing at
# src/lir/lower/calls.rs:364 and is filed as a follow-up separate
# from this track's scope).

void main():
    Dict[String, int] m = {"a": 1, "b": 2}
    # Compare .has (protocol method) vs .has_key (oracle alias): both
    # resolve at type check. Runtime shape divergence is the pre-
    # existing bug; the type resolution is what this track guards.
    print(m.has("a"))           # true
    print(m.has_key("a"))       # pre-existing bug: prints "0"; the
                                # POINT is it TYPES + LINKS.
    print(m.contains("b"))      # true
    print(m.contains_key("b"))  # pre-existing bug: prints "0"
